The page now exposes `#device-platform` and `#device-os` whose text content reflects the live `platform` and `operatingSystem` returned by `Device.getInfo()`. On the web target, `platform` will be `"web"` and `operatingSystem` will be one of `"ios" | "android" | "windows" | "mac" | "unknown"` based on the user agent.
